{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.interfering_block_beats_multiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.interfering_block_beats_multiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.lean#L177-L186","doc":"**The interference threshold, assembled.**  An interfering block (submodular, positive\nbase, damping bonds) has joint factor strictly below the multiplicative prediction:\n`r_ab < r_a·r_b`.  The two bonds must jointly suppress the block *more* than the product of\ntheir separate suppressions — the opposite direction from \"weaker than multiplicative\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.frechet_le_multiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.frechet_le_multiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.lean#L170-L175","doc":"**The Fréchet bound is below the multiplicative one**, with gap exactly `(1−r_a)(1−r_b)`.\nHence \"beats multiplicative damping\" is *strictly weaker* than \"interferes\": a block must\ndamp more strongly than `r_a·r_b` — by at least that gap — before it can turn submodular. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.block_submodular_iff_below_frechet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.block_submodular_iff_below_frechet","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.lean#L161-L168","doc":"**Submodular ⟺ strictly below the Fréchet lower bound** (for a block of positive base).\nThis is the exact characterisation of an interfering block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.frechet_lower_bound_supermodular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.frechet_lower_bound_supermodular","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.lean#L150-L159","doc":"**The Fréchet lower bound forces supermodularity.**  If the joint damping factor obeys\n`r_ab ≥ r_a + r_b − 1` — the Fréchet–Hoeffding lower bound, which any genuine joint survival\nprobability satisfies — then the block is supermodular (`Δ² ≥ 0`), whatever `r_a, r_b` are.\n\nSo an interfering block must **violate the Fréchet lower bound**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.secondDiff_damping","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.secondDiff_damping","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.lean#L145-L148","doc":"A block in damping-factor coordinates: `Δ² = c·(r_ab − r_a − r_b + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.submodular_needs_interfering_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.submodular_needs_interfering_block","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.lean#L120-L136","doc":"**A submodular total forces an interfering block.**  Contrapositive of the class\nexclusion, stated for an arbitrary block decomposition: if the Wedderburn sum is submodular\n(`Δ²g < 0`, the only regime in which `μ₃ > 0` is reachable), then **some** block `λ` has its\nown `Δ²` negative.\n\nThis is the concrete residual target.  Since a per-block multiplicatively-damped block has\n`Δ² = c_λ(1−r_a)(1−r_b) ≥ 0`, an interfering block is precisely one where the two bonds\ndamp **sub-multiplicatively** — the joint effect weaker than the product of the separate\neffects.  The open question is therefore no longer \"find a submodular operator\" but\n\"exhibit intra-block bond interference in a single Wedderburn block\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.mu3_ne_blockwise_multiplicative_cluster","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.mu3_ne_blockwise_multiplicative_cluster","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.lean#L103-L116","doc":"**`μ₃ > 0` is unreachable by any per-block multiplicatively-damped block-trace.**\nThe connected cluster of such a trace is `c₃ = −E₀·Δ²g ≤ 0`, so it cannot equal a positive\nresidual moment.  Scope-(b): a structural exclusion of the entire class, not a measurement\nof one operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.blockwise_multiplicative_supermodular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.blockwise_multiplicative_supermodular","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.lean#L85-L101","doc":"**The class exclusion.**  If every Wedderburn block is multiplicatively damped by the\ntwo bonds — block `λ` contributing `c_λ`, `c_λ r_{λ,a}`, `c_λ r_{λ,b}`, `c_λ r_{λ,a} r_{λ,b}`\nwith `c_λ ≥ 0` and each damping factor `≤ 1` — then the **total** block-trace is\nsupermodular (`Δ²g ≥ 0`).\n\nNote the damping factors may differ **per block**, which is what makes this strictly wider\nthan `Mu3ClusterModularity.multiplicative_supermodular` (a single global pair).  Note also\nthat `0 ≤ r` is *not* needed: only `r ≤ 1`, i.e. that each bond damps rather than amplifies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.secondDiff_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.secondDiff_sum","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.lean#L74-L81","doc":"**`Δ²` commutes with finite sums.**  The second mixed difference of a block-decomposed\ntrace is the sum of the per-block second differences.  This is the whole engine: the\nWedderburn sum `g = Σ_λ (block λ)` has `Δ²g = Σ_λ Δ²(block λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}